   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi<br><br>Right now there are 3 good options, using general bayesian programs that you can call from R. You would need to write your model, there are not easy syntax.<br><br>The programs are:<br>-Stan: <a href=\"http://mc-stan.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mc-stan.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792430922522000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1urFS3nlM5YQ9Tgy8sPT_-\">http://mc-stan.org/</a> (my personal favorite)<br>-JAGS: <a href=\"http://sourceforge.net/projects/mcmc-jags/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sourceforge.net/projects/mcmc-jags/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792430922522000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OOOO7mzgbjlS2OLnb1hjV\">http://sourceforge.net/projects/mcmc-jags/</a><br>-OpenBUGS: <a href=\"http://www.openbugs.net/w/FrontPage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.openbugs.net/w/FrontPage&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792430922522000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0-ecCaBiY3bOZisLpBaHxB\">http://www.openbugs.net/w/FrontPage</a><br><br>A good book resource about this is<span> Basic and Advanced Bayesian Structural Equation Modeling</span> (<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Advanced-Bayesian-Structural-Equation-Modeling/dp/0470669527/ref=sr_1_2?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1412911019&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=bayesian+structural+equation+modeling\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.amazon.com/Advanced-Bayesian-Structural-Equation-Modeling/dp/0470669527/ref%3Dsr_1_2?s%3Dbooks%26ie%3DUTF8%26qid%3D1412911019%26sr%3D1-2%26keywords%3Dbayesian%2Bstructural%2Bequation%2Bmodeling&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792430922522000&amp;usg=AOvVaw17fj68Kx4f5bfzMz6mjmvo\">http://www.amazon.com/Advanced-Bayesian-Structural-Equation-Modeling/dp/0470669527/ref=sr_1_2?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1412911019&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=bayesian+structural+equation+modeling</a>), it has code in WinBUGS that is the older version of OpenBUGS.<br><br>bye</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Thursday, October 9, 2014 5:04:13 PM UTC-5, Koko wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" lang=\"EN-US\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"> </span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Is there a good resource for doing Bayesian SEM in R?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Thanks,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">-K-</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p></div></div></blockquote></div>"
